==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
Derived from {{m|la|querquētum||oak forest}}, from {{m|la|quercus||oak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|querquētulānus}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|querquētulānus}}

# [[oak]]-[[forested]]; covered by an oak [[forest]]

====Declension====
{{la-adecl|querquētulānus}}

====Usage notes====
'''Mōns Querquētulānus''' is an old name of the [[w:Caelian Hill|Caelian Hill]], one of the seven hills of Rome.

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|la|querquētum||wood of oaks}}, from {{suffix|la|quercus|ētum|t1=oak-tree|t2=plantation {{non-gloss definition|or}} grove}}, following [[Auckland]], from {{der|en|enm|ak||oak}} + {{m|en|land}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|querquētulānus}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|querquētulānus}}

#{{lb|la|New Latin}} [[Auckland]], [[New Zealand]]

